            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "VIVNIDHI"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is an excellent recipe. In fact I didn't remove the fennel seeds cause I like their crunch in the salad.Indians make a similar chutney in which they use the same spices and some white sugar&amp; then cook the tomatoes till they are very soft but this tasted really different &amp; good.Thanks for the recipe."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "France C"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Fantastic flavors! This is a nice change from the usual caprese-type salads. I love the bit of heat from the chile pepper infused oil. The fennel was a nice touch, but the cilantro really makes the dish. Use a flaky salt and fresh cracked pepper for best flavor. So simple, but can totally be served to dinner guests to impress!",
            "datePublished": "2025-06-09T01:04:11.690Z"
